{"id": "EUVD-2026-103878", "enisaUuid": "19932d3f-2e36-33c4-aa8b-7ee69f222149", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: bpf: reject invalid NAT manipulation types\n\nAs bpf_ct_set_nat_info() is not validating the NAT manipulation type a\nwrong value can be passed directly to nf_nat_setup_info(). This triggers\nthe WARN_ON() at nf_nat_setup_info() and if panic_on_warn isn't set,\nthen IPS_SRC_NAT_DONE is set without adding nat_bysource and conntrack\ncleanup tries to unlink an uninitialized hlist node.\n\nFix this by checking that NAT manipulation type is correct before\ncalling nf_nat_setup_info(). In addition, if the WARN_ON is hit, return\nNF_DROP instead of continuing with the processing to avoid similar\nsituations in the future.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:48:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:57:02", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/752492947be3123ea6c689e2f93ae04ecd675d42", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ea777dc90ab37e64fa4b92f6fcf3b5edcef5e058", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f6143ae109df56d51d5536e813deb19eee7a6205", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/58108f05b0502448f6bb612ee2eccc63bd6449cb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/16d464013ec2267b00a83f4bfbb97b3ecc63bfa7"], "aliases": ["GHSA-g33v-6845-q9px", "CVE-2026-98793"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "08fefe8b-adbf-354b-8a83-387331f9ba4a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "154595fc-92e0-3fe9-b751-2bf4d89e4424", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0fabd2aa199faeb8754aee94658f2c48ccb2c8c3 <16d464013ec2267b00a83f4bfbb97b3ecc63bfa7"}, {"id": "601fb886-5204-397c-922e-2de6a2575d3c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "641e20b1-809a-3360-98c3-278ca854d23a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1"}, {"id": "7de93fd2-4d4e-300f-b4ea-c91638b61e70", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0fabd2aa199faeb8754aee94658f2c48ccb2c8c3 <752492947be3123ea6c689e2f93ae04ecd675d42"}, {"id": "80913a50-d904-3885-b77b-59d704969e38", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "a7e4932b-90c3-3a31-80c5-b83b348de8f5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0fabd2aa199faeb8754aee94658f2c48ccb2c8c3 <58108f05b0502448f6bb612ee2eccc63bd6449cb"}, {"id": "b358b264-1529-3062-83a3-7a0d313a923e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0fabd2aa199faeb8754aee94658f2c48ccb2c8c3 <ea777dc90ab37e64fa4b92f6fcf3b5edcef5e058"}, {"id": "b9b2c707-7990-3072-b1ae-744ddedb8cd4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0fabd2aa199faeb8754aee94658f2c48ccb2c8c3 <f6143ae109df56d51d5536e813deb19eee7a6205"}, {"id": "bf49de08-7450-3804-b233-62a3f2400762", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "dd39626b-dfb7-35a7-9145-94ce7573ae10", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "ef09cc95-74a6-3352-b77f-551e9b1b5206", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6eddc66e-663c-34ee-9764-c8878d981650", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}